#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:201
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "All swarm slots have drained or halted cleanly, final Dual Scoreboard and Milestone Rollup is published, and shared work-plan state is synced."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:41
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Background workers operating in isolated git worktrees, one disjoint slice and one sub-bean per worker. Each worker emits live progress and completion blocks with command output tails, exit codes, and commit SHAs, and pushes its branch without merging."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:194
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Cancel any remaining wakeup timer and run Process_BeanClose on the swarm epic: complete and archive when all sub-beans landed, or record explicit blockers/owner decisions in beans and hand back cleanly."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:187
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Claim the next unblocked sub-beans in the shared beans store (pushing claims to the branch store), dispatch fresh isolated-worktree workers into freed slots, and re-arm the 2-to-4-minute one-shot fallback timer before ending the turn."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:104
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Claim the parent swarm epic and initial worker sub-beans in the shared beans store through Process_BeanOpen and push state to the branch store so sibling sessions see every active claim."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:193
#. Diagram label
msgid "Close or park swarm epic"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:30
#. Diagram label
msgid "Coordinator"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:84
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Coordinator posts the full context, worker count, model tiers, relative token cost, options, and recommendation in chat, followed immediately by a tappable card; the owner approves or declines."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:83
#. Diagram label
msgid "Decide swarm card"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:68
#. Diagram label
msgid "Decompose disjoint sub-beans"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:31
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Decomposes the goal into disjoint sub-beans in the shared work-plan store, verifies or requests swarm-spawn permission, opens the parent swarm work item through Process_BeanOpen, and dispatches isolated-worktree workers with the progress contract and an armed fallback timer."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:111
#. Diagram label
msgid "Dispatch workers and arm timer"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:21
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Dispatches parallel isolated-worktree worker agents against disjoint sub-beans under an approved or waived swarm-spawn gate, then supervises them on reactive completion wakeups and a 2-to-4-minute fallback timer until the queue drains or halts. Each monitor sweep extracts live progress blocks, measures repository queues and host CPU, disk, and compressed or swapped memory footprint, intervenes on stalls or runaway subprocess leaks, publishes a self-contained Dual Scoreboard and Milestone/Epic Progress Rollup free of internal shorthands, hands independently verified pull requests to the merge steward, and refills freed worker slots from the shared work plan."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:226
#. Diagram label
msgid "Drained"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:119
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Each worker executes its claimed disjoint slice in its worktree, tees long commands to logs, emits live progress blocks every ~90 seconds and at each step, runs verification, pushes its branch and draft/ready PR, and emits a final DONE block without merging."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:118
#. Diagram label
msgid "Execute slice and emit progress"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:27
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Grants or declines per-swarm spawn permission on a tappable decision card after reading worker count, model tiers, and relative token cost in chat, unless a bounded swarm-spawn waiver already covers the scope."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:165
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Hand the verified six-line merge request (or ready-to-merge / needs-repin label) to the active merge steward for batch approval and merge-train landing; neither workers nor monitor self-merge outside the merge-steward lane."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:142
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Immediately SIGKILL any runaway subprocess leaking into compressed memory or swapfiles and message its worker; nudge a silent worker via SendMessage; route dead sessions through stalled-agent-triage; or pull the Andon cord to halt remaining workers on structural divergence or host exhaustion."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:172
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Join after optional merge-steward handoff before evaluating remaining worker slots and queued beans."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:112
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Launch workers in isolated git worktrees with the verbatim progress contract, governing skill paths, interaction-modality and hand-back-to-discussion rules, and CPU thread caps; arm the 2-to-4-minute one-shot fallback wakeup timer."
msgstr ""

