#. Diagram label
msgid "Merge steward"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:207
#. Diagram label
msgid "No"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:141
#. Diagram label
msgid "Nudge, kill leak or pull Andon"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:103
#. Diagram label
msgid "Open the swarm epic"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:26
#. Diagram label
msgid "Owner"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:63
#. Diagram label
msgid "Parallel work requested"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:148
#. Diagram label
msgid "Publish scoreboard and rollup"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:164
#. Diagram label
msgid "Queue PR in merge watch"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:58
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Receives six-line merge requests for independently verified pull requests and routes them through the merge train or direct merge guard under the owner's batch approval."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:186
#. Diagram label
msgid "Refill slots and re-arm timer"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:98
#. Diagram label
msgid "Run serially"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:178
#. Diagram label
msgid "Slots active or refillable?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:90
#. Diagram label
msgid "Spawn approved?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:133
#. Diagram label
msgid "Stall, drift or swap leak?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:200
#. Diagram label
msgid "Swarm closed"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:99
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Swarm declined or unjustified; work proceeds sequentially one sub-bean at a time."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:18
#. Diagram label
msgid "Swarm dispatch and monitor"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:44
#. Diagram label
msgid "Swarm monitor"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:75
#. Diagram label
msgid "Swarm-spawn waived?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:126
#. Diagram label
msgid "Sweep progress, queues and swap"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:149
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Synthesize a self-contained human status update with zero naked worker codes, bare PR ranges, or unglossed bean IDs: (A) Live Repository Queue Scoreboard across PRs, Work Items, and Issues, and (B) Milestone and Epic Progress Rollups stating the track goal, landed verified results with metrics, ready PR summaries, and active/queued work."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:64
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Two or more independent workstreams are candidates for parallel background execution, or the owner asks to drain an epic with monitored workers."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:156
#. Diagram label
msgid "Verified PR ready?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:69
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Verify that a swarm is justified over serial execution (swarm-management), partition the work into sub-beans with non-overlapping writable paths and explicit Done-when criteria in the shared beans store, and size worker count, model tiers (cost-aware routing), and host concurrency bounds."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:45
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Wakes on worker completion events or a 2-to-4-minute fallback timer without busy-polling: extracts live progress, checks CPU load, root disk headroom, and compressed or swapped memory footprint, kills runaway leaks or pulls the Andon cord on structural defects, publishes anti-shorthand queue scoreboards and milestone rollups, sends verified ready pull requests to the merge steward, refills freed worker slots from beans, and closes out through Process_BeanClose when drained."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:127
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Woken reactively by worker completion/messages or by the 2-to-4-minute fallback timer: run the targeted JSONL progress extractor, query live forge PR/issue counts and synced beans states, and inspect CPU load, root disk free space (df -h /), and total plus compressed/swap memory (top -l 1 -o mem -stats pid,command,mem,cmprs on macOS or VmRSS + VmSwap on Linux, never ps -o rss alone)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:40
#. Diagram label
msgid "Worker agents"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:208
#. Diagram label
msgid "Yes"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:157
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Yes when a completed worker branch passes independent parent verification (typecheck, tests, and applicable gates) and is ready for merge-steward intake. No when workers are still running or blocked."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:76
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Yes when an active owner confirmation waiver explicitly covers swarm-spawn up to this worker count and model tier, quoted in the turn report. No otherwise: ask first, per swarm."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:134
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Yes when any worker subprocess breaches the memory+compressed/swap or root-disk floor, a worker is silent for over 3 minutes or repeats step counters across two sweeps, workers collide on a path, or completed slices diverge structurally. No when all workers and host headroom are healthy."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:91
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Yes when the owner approves the swarm card. No when declined: fall back to sequential execution."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:179
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Yes while workers remain live or unclaimed, unblocked sub-beans remain in the shared beans queue with healthy host headroom and no Andon halt. Drained when all sub-beans are completed, parked on an owner decision card, or halted by the Andon cord."
msgstr ""
